Falsifies `system_tests::user::std_threads_tests::four_std_threads_share_a_mutex_an_atomic_and_a_space`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect, in milestone 812 (`std::thread::spawn` runs real threads in one address space): a thread that joins a process is not given the thread pointer `CONFIGURE`
carried, so every `std` thread the program spawns starts with none, and thread-local storage is
not its own.

Expected to fail: the program ends before its output does. On aarch64 and riscv64 every spawned
thread finds the main thread's block and `std` aborts ("current thread handle already set during
thread spawn"); on `x86_64` a spawned thread faults reading `fs:[0]`, which ends the process.

diff --git a/kernel/src/sched/configure.rs b/kernel/src/sched/configure.rs
